captured-0030-phy-212-119291668,2053526,PHY-212,119291668,obj-phy-212-download-119291668,dl-phy-212-0045|dl-phy-212-0097|dl-phy-212-0101|dl-phy-212-0102,download-0045|download-0097|download-0101|download-0102,/Users/jake/Developer/SU26/canvas/indexer/output/downloaded_files/PHY-212_119291668_M1-01.pdf,/Users/jake/Developer/SU26/canvas/indexer/output/parsed_files/captured-0030-phy-212-119291668.md,parsed,manual-vision-override,pdf,1,669,9cb30947ef98199b212aa9ef8fe8435166dc52f38e6657b3751507c47dd1cad9,PHY-212_119291668_M1-01.pdf,"# M1-01 Header: M1-01; Jacob Peterson; student ID visible on page. ## Problem 1 omega_F = omega_I + alpha t 0 = 12 + alpha(26) alpha = -12 / 26 = -0.4615 rad/s^2 Magnitude: |alpha| = 0.46 rad/s^2 ## Problem 2 The disk is initially spinning counterclockwise, so by the right-hand rule, omega points out of the page. Since the disk is slowing down, alpha points opposite to omega. Answer: into the page ## Problem 3 Average angular speed: omega_avg = (omega_I + omega_F) / 2 = (12 + 0) / 2 = 6 rad/s Angular displacement: Delta theta = omega_avg t = (6)(26) = 156 rad Convert to revolutions: 156 rad (1 rev / 2 pi rad) = 24.83 rev Answer: 25 revolutions",2026-06-26T23:45:13.796984+00:00,Manual transcription from rendered PDF image because PDF text extraction returned empty text.
captured-0031-phy-212-119284452,2053526,PHY-212,119284452,obj-phy-212-download-119284452,dl-phy-212-0044|dl-phy-212-0098|dl-phy-212-0099|dl-phy-212-0100,download-0044|download-0098|download-0099|download-0100,/Users/jake/Developer/SU26/canvas/indexer/output/downloaded_files/PHY-212_119284452_M1-00.pdf,/Users/jake/Developer/SU26/canvas/indexer/output/parsed_files/captured-0031-phy-212-119284452.md,parsed,manual-vision-override,pdf,1,460,66adfa8624d0c0e09635c710b96ded258d290aa3db5aa8a30acf40372f103c79,PHY-212_119284452_M1-00.pdf,# M1-00 Header: M1-00; Jacob Peterson; student ID visible on page. ## Problem 1 Set angular velocity to zero when it reverses direction: 0 = A - B t^2 t = sqrt(A / B) = sqrt(18 / 0.50) = sqrt(36) = 6.0 Answer: 6.0 ## Problem 2 The disk reverses at t = 6.0 s. Angular displacement: Delta theta = integral from 0 to 6 of (A - B t^2) dt Delta theta = A t - (B / 3) t^3 Delta theta = 18(6.0) - (0.50 / 3)(6.0)^3 Delta theta = 108 - 36 = 72 Answer: 72,2026-06-26T23:45:13.796984+00:00,Manual transcription from rendered PDF image because PDF text extraction returned empty text.
